	(text "POWER  —  Power tree: VSYS input, regulators, AUX IN pass-through and monitoring  —  HW 0.1.0-proto.1" (at 40 20 0) (effects (font (size 4 4) (thickness 0.6)) (justify left)))
	(rectangle (start 30.48 41.91) (end 508.0 172.72) (stroke (width 0.15) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "81192223-214d-a640-9a7c-52e6554e498e"))
	(text "input OR-ing" (at 33.02 45.72 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (thickness 0.3)) (justify left)))
	(text "Where power enters. Two inputs feed one internal supply, VSYS: USB-C (5 V, or 9 V when a USB-PD charger agrees) and the J50 screw terminal (9-21 V). A diode on each (D3, D4) lets whichever is higher supply the board and stops one input from back-feeding the other. On the USB side, U26 is an electronic fuse: it ramps the voltage\nup gently so plugging in does not spark, cuts off above about 10 V or below 3.75 V, and limits current to about 2 A. D8 clamps voltage spikes on the screw input. VSYS then feeds the two main regulators." (at 33.02 50.8 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) (italic yes)) (justify left top)))
	(rectangle (start 30.48 193.04) (end 378.46 321.31) (stroke (width 0.15) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "87d91be8-3614-a6f7-db7b-f1c92f2afa87"))
	(text "U11  VSYS to +5V" (at 33.02 196.85 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (thickness 0.3)) (justify left)))
	(text "Switching regulator (buck converter) that makes +5V from VSYS. It runs whenever power is present (no enable), like U12, so the FPGA's 1.8 V auxiliary supply is never missing while its 3.3 V banks are powered. Its output goes to the +5V\nrail through U34. +5V feeds the 5 V buses, the extension 5 V pins and the four small regulators below. The two feedback resistors set the output voltage; the inductor and capacitors are its power stage; the 10 uF across its input is its\nown switching-current reservoir." (at 33.02 201.93 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) (italic yes)) (justify left top)))
	(rectangle (start 389.89 193.04) (end 737.87 318.77) (stroke (width 0.15) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "4cabdbca-e616-f71f-350f-1d12241f2699"))
	(text "U12  VSYS to +3V3  (always on)" (at 392.43 196.85 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (thickness 0.3)) (justify left)))
	(text "Switching regulator that makes +3V3 from VSYS. It has no enable: it starts as soon as any power is present, because +3V3 runs the board controller, which then switches everything else on. Also powers the PSRAM, the flashes, the PHY and\nmost logic. The two feedback resistors set 3.3 V; the inductor and capacitors are its power stage; the 1 uF on VCC feeds its own control circuit." (at 392.43 201.93 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) (italic yes)) (justify left top)))
	(rectangle (start 30.48 340.36) (end 312.42 448.31) (stroke (width 0.15) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "6a18f406-4b40-d9c8-3127-e5630a70afea"))
	(text "U13  5V to +2V5" (at 33.02 344.17 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (thickness 0.3)) (justify left)))
	(text "Small switching regulator that makes +2V5 from +5V for FPGA bank 16 (network) and the PHY's RGMII pins. Enabled by the board controller (EN_2V5); the feedback resistors set 2.5 V." (at 33.02 349.25 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) (italic yes)) (justify left top)))
	(rectangle (start 323.85 340.36) (end 572.77 453.39) (stroke (width 0.15) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "101547a0-cfc0-5da4-e527-af55f21ccdb7"))
	(text "U14  5V to +1V8_IO" (at 326.39 344.17 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (thickness 0.3)) (justify left)))
	(text "Small switching regulator that makes 1.8 V from +5V. Its output node is +1V8_IO: FPGA bank 13 and the 1.8 V memory on it, the 1.8 V position of the J19/J20 jumpers, and,\nthrough the bead below, the FPGA's auxiliary supply (VCCAUX) and its ADC as +1V8. Its enable is tied to +5V, so it runs whenever U11 does: the FPGA's 3.3 V banks are\nnever left on an unpowered VCCAUX (DS181 Table 7). The feedback resistors set 1.8 V; the 4.7 uF at VIN is its own input reservoir." (at 326.39 349.25 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) (italic yes)) (justify left top)))
	(rectangle (start 30.48 473.71) (end 345.44 584.2) (stroke (width 0.15) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "3230a9a4-976c-7fb7-38f1-b844c6e84944"))
	(text "U15  5V to +1V0  (4A FPGA core supply)" (at 33.02 477.52 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (thickness 0.3)) (justify left)))
	(text "The FPGA core supply: up to 4 A at 1.0 V from +5V, the heaviest rail on the board. Enabled by the board controller (EN_1V0) once +5V is settled above its 4.5 V minimum; firmware watches the rail through MON_1V0 (the\npart has no power-good pin). The feedback resistors set 1.0 V; the bootstrap capacitor feeds its high-side driver." (at 33.02 482.6 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) (italic yes)) (justify left top)))
	(rectangle (start 356.87 473.71) (end 524.51 539.75) (stroke (width 0.15) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "34b3a70f-8334-5377-f408-13de55b85b31"))
	(text "extension power protection control" (at 359.41 477.52 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (thickness 0.3)) (justify left)))
	(text "Shared control for the four protected extension supplies (U21-U24). EXT_EN, from the board controller, turns\nthem all on; the pull-down keeps them off until firmware decides. EXT_FAULT is pulled up and goes low if any of\nthem (or the USB eFuse) detects a fault, so one controller pin hears all of them." (at 359.41 482.6 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) (italic yes)) (justify left top)))
	(rectangle (start 537.21 473.71) (end 704.85 586.74) (stroke (width 0.15) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "c72c9fb2-6008-ac11-d91c-d1d956a148be"))
	(text "U21  +5V to +5V_EXT" (at 539.75 477.52 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (thickness 0.3)) (justify left)))
	(text "Protected switch between the board's +5V and the 5 V pins of every extension port. Limits current to about 1 A\nand blocks current flowing back from an extension. Without it, a shorted extension would pull the whole board's\n5 V down." (at 539.75 482.6 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) (italic yes)) (justify left top)))
	(rectangle (start 30.48 607.06) (end 198.12 716.28) (stroke (width 0.15) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "2e1a995d-1856-4644-d1f0-6a2a185310b1"))
	(text "U22  +3V3 to +3V3_EXT" (at 33.02 610.87 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (thickness 0.3)) (justify left)))
	(text "Protected switch between +3V3 and the 3.3 V pins of every extension port, limited to about 0.5 A, with reverse\nblocking. Keeps a faulty extension from taking down the board controller's supply." (at 33.02 615.95 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) (italic yes)) (justify left top)))
	(rectangle (start 209.55 607.06) (end 378.46 726.44) (stroke (width 0.15) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "5e5f7fcf-a1d4-2d9d-a61e-60cbb45b11b9"))
	(text "U23  VCCIO_1 to VCCIO_1_EXT" (at 212.09 610.87 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (thickness 0.3)) (justify left)))
	(text "Switch for the PIN V supply of slots A-D (the voltage chosen on J19). It is biased from +3V3 so it works down to\nthe 1.8 V setting, blocks current flowing back in while off, ramps its output in about 1.5 ms and shuts down\nwhen hot. Overload protection is each slot's 500 mA fuse; the switch itself has no current limit." (at 212.09 615.95 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) (italic yes)) (justify left top)))
	(rectangle (start 389.89 607.06) (end 557.53 726.44) (stroke (width 0.15) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "d1b93ab0-60db-d3c8-73de-5a7d49335efb"))
	(text "U24  VCCIO_2 to VCCIO_2_EXT" (at 392.43 610.87 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (thickness 0.3)) (justify left)))
	(text "Switch for the PIN V supply of slots E-H (the voltage chosen on J20). It is biased from +3V3 so it works down to\nthe 1.8 V setting, blocks current flowing back in while off, ramps its output in about 1.5 ms and shuts down\nwhen hot. Overload protection is each slot's 500 mA fuse; the switch itself has no current limit." (at 392.43 615.95 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) (italic yes)) (justify left top)))
	(rectangle (start 30.48 746.76) (end 642.62 810.26) (stroke (width 0.15) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "cf1a4f2d-b21a-6c00-ec91-376d02e46913"))
	(text "rail monitors" (at 33.02 750.57 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (thickness 0.3)) (justify left)))
	(text "Lets the board controller measure every supply. Each rail goes to one of its eight analog inputs (ADC), which read 0-3.3 V. Rails at or below 3.3 V go through a 1 k resistor that protects the pin; VSYS and +5V are higher, so two resistors divide them down first. A 100 nF capacitor on each input steadies the reading. MON_1V8 reads +1V8 itself, the FPGA's VCCAUX behind the bead, so an open bead shows; the two jumpered\ndomains are measured so firmware knows how J19/J20 are set. Firmware uses this to check each regulator came up before enabling the next." (at 33.02 755.65 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) (italic yes)) (justify left top)))
	(rectangle (start 30.48 830.58) (end 198.12 890.27) (stroke (width 0.15) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "dd6b19f4-23c2-07f7-e43e-2e021e9113f4"))
	(text "AUX IN" (at 33.02 834.39 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (thickness 0.3)) (justify left)))
	(text "Optional extra power for extensions that need more than 5 V (motors, LED strips, displays). Whatever you connect\nhere (9-28 V DC) goes, unregulated, to the AUX pin of every extension port through each port's own fuse. The\nboard itself never uses it." (at 33.02 839.47 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) (italic yes)) (justify left top)))
	(rectangle (start 209.55 830.58) (end 378.46 900.43) (stroke (width 0.15) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "18d682c0-eb87-a9a8-8330-8ea3edd58f41"))
	(text "VCCAUX filter" (at 212.09 834.39 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (thickness 0.3)) (justify left)))
	(text "The split between +1V8_IO and +1V8. VCCAUX and VCCADC are the FPGA's internal supplies (clocking, I/O pre-\ndrivers, the XADC) and should not share copper with switching 1.8 V I/O loads, so they hang off U14's output\nthrough one ferrite bead (120 ohm at 100 MHz, 2 A, 50 mohm: 9 mV at the 0.18 A VCCAUX allowance, inside VCCAUX's\n1.71 V minimum). The 10 uF and 100 nF sit at U14's output beside its own capacitors; VCCAUX keeps its UG483\ndecoupling on the +1V8 side." (at 212.09 839.47 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) (italic yes)) (justify left top)))
	(rectangle (start 30.48 920.75) (end 477.52 1041.4) (stroke (width 0.15) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "42566e98-661f-7152-c8d2-58d3771fe48e"))
	(text "U34  +5V source select" (at 33.02 924.56 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (thickness 0.3)) (justify left)))
	(text "Chooses what feeds the +5V rail: USB power straight from the connector, or U11. A regulator cannot make 5 V out of 5 V, so on a plain 5 V USB source the mux passes VBUS to the rail. It hands the rail to U11 while the board controller asks the charger for 9 V and for a few seconds after (Q6), while the screw\ninput is powered (Q7), and, as a backstop, if VBUS rises above about 5.6 V unasked or goes away. The choice is wired, not firmware: dividers and two small transistors. The chip blocks current flowing backwards into either source, limits the rail current to about 2.5 A and ramps it up gently. ST tells the\nboard controller which source is in use." (at 33.02 929.64 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) (italic yes)) (justify left top)))
	(rectangle (start 488.95 920.75) (end 656.59 989.33) (stroke (width 0.15) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "8d769549-4da8-ab31-5f06-6fbb587dd778"))
	(text "Q6  mux hold: 9 V request" (at 491.49 924.56 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (thickness 0.3)) (justify left)))
	(text "Keeps U34 on U11 around a 9 V negotiation. The controller's 9 V request charges a capacitor through D24 at once\nand the capacitor drains through its resistor in 2-7 s, so the rail leaves VBUS before the charger moves it and\nreturns only when VBUS is back at 5 V. No voltage threshold can do that within the tolerances involved." (at 491.49 929.64 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) (italic yes)) (justify left top)))
	(rectangle (start 30.48 1061.72) (end 198.12 1127.76) (stroke (width 0.15) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "264c09ae-6d59-64d2-3db5-563ce1f2e319"))
	(text "Q7  mux hold: screw input present" (at 33.02 1065.53 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (thickness 0.3)) (justify left)))
	(text "Keeps U34 on U11 whenever the screw input carries voltage, so a bench supply on J50 carries the whole board even\nwith a 5 V USB cable plugged in; before, the USB port kept the 5 V load." (at 33.02 1070.61 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) (italic yes)) (justify left top)))
